{"availability":"available","full":"edkedk99/streamlit_sql","name":"streamlit_sql","description":"CRUD interface for sqlalchemy using streamlit","category":"Other","language":"Python","stars":26,"forks":7,"created":"2024-12-04T14:17:13Z","updated":"2025-03-25T17:44:54Z","branch":"master","homepage":"https://edkedk99.github.io/streamlit_sql/","topics":["crud","sqlalchemy","streamlit","streamlit-component"],"demo":"https://example-crud.streamlit.app/","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T21:28:46.879Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-08T21:28:46.879Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-08T21:28:46.879Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-08T21:28:46.879Z","stars":26,"forks":7}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Creating a CRUD interface can be a tedious and repetitive task. This package is intended to replace all of that with a few lines of code that involves simply creating a sqlalchemy statement and calling the main SqlUi class with only 3 required arguments. All extra and advanced features are available by supplying non-required arguments to the class initialization.","When the main class is initialized, it will display the database table data with most of the expected features of a crud interface, so the user will be able to read, filter, update, create and delete rows with many useful features.","It also offers useful information about the data as property like:"],"features":["df: The Dataframe displayed in the screen","selectedrows: The position of selected rows. This is not the row id","qttyrows: The quantity of all rows after filtering","Display as a regular st.dataframe","Add pagination, displaying only a set of rows each time"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/edkedk99/streamlit_sql/blob/master/README.md","fingerprint":"63b2755e5556102510c4af0a6a52207e54a2c830903944d085cc006acd6253b2","extractedAt":"2026-10-08T21:28:46.984Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T21:28:46.984Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDo